MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The step drill bits felt like a natural next choice because they would help me enlarge sheet-metal holes for the rivets and rivet nuts I have been buying.",
    "The mounting tape fits my repeated use of adhesives and fasteners, giving me another way to secure parts when screws are impractical. Duct tape also fits my frequent repair work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The valves require particular tubing, hose, or PVC connections and an actual project needing them; my fastening work does not establish those needs.",
    "Printer resin does not serve the same purpose as my tabletop epoxy, and owning measurement tools does not mean I currently need sound-level testing. Breadboards likewise lack a connection to my recent mechanical work."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop supplies seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any repair or fabrication product.",
    "Shared words such as resin or broad similarities such as measuring seem to count more than whether the products accomplish the same task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts, and drilling tools point toward fastening and preparing parts for assembly, which makes complementary tools especially useful.",
    "Exact dimensions and current project needs matter: the deck screws are relevant to my interests, but I would wait until I needed that length for outdoor woodwork. Frequent workshop activity does not make every specialized supply useful now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my fastening and repair interests but extended them too far into specialized tasks and materials I have no current reason to use."
}
